# Wall of Voices environment
#
# Every variable here is OPTIONAL. The wall asks the visitor for a Speechmatics
# key in the browser and exchanges it for a short-lived realtime key, so nothing
# here has to be set for the wall to run.
#
# Local: copy this file to .env next to it. dev_server.py and cli.py both read
# it; .env is gitignored, this file is the one that gets committed.

# --- Optional: dev-only server key ------------------------------------------

# A Speechmatics API key, from https://portal.speechmatics.com/ under API Keys,
# with access to the Melia preview. Set it and dev_server.py will use it when the
# browser sends no key, so you can work locally without pasting one. cli.py needs
# it too. Set nothing and the browser path is the only path.
#
# KEEP THIS ON YOUR OWN MACHINE. api/token.py never reads the environment; it
# mints only against a key the caller supplied. Putting a key where the token
# endpoint is reachable by anyone would hand out Speechmatics credentials
# against your account to whoever finds the URL, which is the thing
# browser-supplied keys exist to prevent.
#
# Never commit it, never log it, never send it to the client.
# SPEECHMATICS_API_KEY=your_api_key_here

# --- Optional: everything else ----------------------------------------------

# Lifetime, in SECONDS, of each temporary key /api/token mints.
#
# Whole integer only. "60" works; "60s" and "1m" do not. Those fall back to the
# default rather than failing outright, so they will not look broken while
# quietly ignoring you. Values outside the API's 60..86400 range are clamped.
#
# The default is the floor on purpose. The temporary key travels in the Melia
# WebSocket URL as a ?jwt= query parameter, because a browser WebSocket cannot
# set an Authorization header, and query strings leak into proxy logs, browser
# history and Referer headers. One key can start any number of sessions for as
# long as it lives. The client mints a fresh key per connection attempt and
# never reuses one, so raising this buys you nothing and costs you containment.
# SM_TOKEN_TTL=60

# Port for dev_server.py, which serves public/ and /api/token together so the
# wall runs locally from one process. Defaults to 3100.
#
# The dev server binds loopback (127.0.0.1) and there is no variable here to
# change that, deliberately: with a key in .env it mints Speechmatics credentials
# against your account for anyone who asks, with no authentication of any kind.
# On conference Wi-Fi, loopback is the only thing between that and a room full
# of laptops.
# PORT=3100
